WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:09.060
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.891
Unit eighteen: Imperatives (commands). Today you will give instructions and orders politely.

4
00:00:15.191 --> 00:00:17.971
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:22.514
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.084
Stop.

7
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:27.536
Stop means to not move or not continue.

8
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.592
Stop at the red light.

9
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:32.371
Your turn. Say: Stop.

10
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:36.107
Stop.

11
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:37.514
Go.

12
00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:40.679
Go means to move to another place.

13
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:42.482
Go to the door.

14
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:45.260
Your turn. Say: Go.

15
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:48.741
Go.

16
00:00:49.483 --> 00:00:50.426
Sit down.

17
00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.347
Sit down means to take a seat.

18
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.172
Please sit down.

19
00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:58.308
Your turn. Say: Sit down.

20
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.086
Sit down.

21
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:03.712
Please.

22
00:01:04.717 --> 00:01:07.157
Please means a polite word for requests.

23
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.355
Open the window, please.

24
00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.568
Your turn. Say: Please.

25
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:16.202
Please.

26
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:17.777
Command.

27
00:01:18.783 --> 00:01:21.445
Command means an order that tells someone what to do.

28
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.038
A command uses the base verb.

29
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.279
Your turn. Say: Command.

30
00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.076
Command.

31
00:01:31.817 --> 00:01:32.945
Instruction.

32
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.971
Instruction means words that tell you how to do something.

33
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:39.525
Read the instruction carefully.

34
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:42.711
Your turn. Say: Instruction.

35
00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:46.649
Instruction.

36
00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:48.431
Don't touch.

37
00:01:49.417 --> 00:01:51.381
Don't touch means a negative command.

38
00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:53.588
Don't touch the hot pot.

39
00:01:54.183 --> 00:01:57.079
Your turn. Say: Don't touch.

40
00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:00.981
Don't touch.

41
00:02:01.717 --> 00:02:02.567
Listen.

42
00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:06.001
Listen means to pay attention to a sound.

43
00:02:06.617 --> 00:02:08.024
Listen to the teacher.

44
00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:11.095
Your turn. Say: Listen.

45
00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:14.865
Listen.

46
00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:19.503
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.371
Visal, what does a teacher say at the start of a class?

48
00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:35.784
Sit down, please. Open your books. Listen. These are imperatives. We use the base verb and no subject. The subject is you, but we do not say it.

49
00:02:36.883 --> 00:02:38.326
How do we make it polite?

50
00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:50.605
Add please at the start or the end: Please sit down, or Sit down, please. We also use a friendly voice. Please is the most important polite word.

51
00:02:51.717 --> 00:02:53.112
And a negative command?

52
00:02:54.217 --> 00:03:03.109
Put don't before the base verb: Don't touch the stove. Don't run in class. Don't is the short form of do not. It warns people.

53
00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:05.732
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:11.125
Grammar focus: Imperatives: base verb and Don't plus base verb.

55
00:03:11.425 --> 00:03:12.670
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.383 --> 00:03:14.570
Please sit down.

57
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:16.821
Open your books.

58
00:03:17.717 --> 00:03:19.287
Don't touch the hot pot.

59
00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:27.788
An imperative uses the base verb and no subject. Add please to be polite. Use don't + base verb for a negative command.

60
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.899
Be careful! Don't say: You sit down, please.

61
00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:35.752
Say: Sit down, please.

62
00:03:36.052 --> 00:03:38.214
Do not use a subject in a command.

63
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.977
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.302
Classroom Rules.

65
00:03:44.602 --> 00:03:46.741
Please sit down and open your books.

66
00:03:47.733 --> 00:03:50.128
Listen to the teacher, and don't talk loudly.

67
00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.086
Go to the board when I call your name.

68
00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.169
Stop writing when the time is over.

69
00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:59.828
Good instructions are clear, short and polite.

70
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:04.656
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.517 --> 00:04:07.087
blank your books, please.

72
00:04:07.387 --> 00:04:10.692
A, Open. B, Opens. C, You open.

73
00:04:14.233 --> 00:04:16.279
The answer is A: Open.

74
00:04:17.417 --> 00:04:19.126
blank run in the classroom.

75
00:04:19.426 --> 00:04:22.371
A, Don't. B, Doesn't. C, Not.

76
00:04:25.933 --> 00:04:27.492
The answer is A: Don't.

77
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.475
Which sentence is a command?

78
00:04:30.775 --> 00:04:36.217
A, She sits down.. B, Sit down, please.. C, I am sitting..

79
00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:42.707
The answer is B: Sit down, please..

80
00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.337
The word that makes a command polite is blank.

81
00:04:46.637 --> 00:04:49.698
A, please. B, stop. C, now.

82
00:04:53.233 --> 00:04:55.117
The answer is A: please.

83
00:04:56.283 --> 00:04:59.618
According to the reading, what should you do when the time is over?

84
00:04:59.918 --> 00:05:04.384
A, stop writing. B, go home. C, talk loudly.

85
00:05:07.933 --> 00:05:10.490
The answer is A: stop writing.

86
00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.852
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:15.717 --> 00:05:19.191
Write three classroom instructions using the imperative form.

88
00:05:27.983 --> 00:05:29.553
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:29.853 --> 00:05:43.395
Open your book. Listen to the teacher. Don't talk loudly. These are classroom instructions. I use the base verb at the start. For a polite command I add please, and for a warning I use don't.

90
00:05:43.695 --> 00:05:45.404
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:46.317 --> 00:05:52.835
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and imperatives: base verb and don't plus base verb.

92
00:05:53.135 --> 00:05:56.623
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

93
00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:59.750
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:03.201
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

